# ============================================================================
# eve-hybrid-agent-template — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development (`.env*` is gitignored except
# this file). On Vercel, set each var on the project — mark every secret as
# Sensitive. Docs: docs/01-prerequisites.md and docs/07-ops.md.
#
# Billing model (docs/00-architecture.md): the eve LOOP bills to Vercel AI
# Gateway; the nested dev-agent (Claude Code in the sandbox) bills to a Claude
# subscription via ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN. The two auth surfaces are disjoint —
# neither credential works on the other layer.
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev-agent auth (REQUIRED for run_dev_task)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude subscription OAuth token from `claude setup-token`. Powers the nested
# Claude Code CLI inside the Vercel Sandbox — the ONLY layer where subscription
# auth works. Mark Sensitive on Vercel. Tokens expire ~1 year after issuance
# and nothing alerts on expiry: record the rotation date somewhere a human
# sees it (docs/01-prerequisites.md).
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=sk-ant-oat01-...

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# eve loop billing (AI Gateway)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed for LOCAL development. On Vercel, omit it — the deployment
# authenticates to the AI Gateway via OIDC automatically. Locally you can also
# use `vercel env pull` to get a VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN instead.
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=vck_...

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Models (all optional — every model id is env-overridable; rollback = unset)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default loop model: the cheap model that handles routing and ordinary turns.
# ORCHESTRATOR_MODEL=google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# Model for command turns (a bot-mention command on a PR). Sonnet over Haiku:
# its prompt-cache reads (1024-token minimum prefix) beat Haiku, whose
# 4096-token minimum silently disables caching for orchestrator-sized prompts.
# Command turns are rare and short-output — the intelligence still lives in
# the nested dev-agent.
# COMMAND_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5

# Nested Claude Code model inside the sandbox (Anthropic-native id format,
# hyphens not dots). Leave unset to use Claude Code's own default.
# DEV_AGENT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub App channel (BYO App — docs/03-github-channel.md)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App id from the GitHub App settings page.
GITHUB_APP_ID=123456

# App private key (PEM). Hosted platforms often \n-escape multiline values —
# agent/lib/github-token.ts normalizes escaped newlines back to real ones.
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----"

# Webhook secret configured on the App (webhook URL: https://<deployment>/eve/v1/github).
GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=...

# Optional: the App's mention handle (slug). Overrides the BOT_NAME constant in
# agent/lib/dispatch.ts — drives both eve's mention dispatch and the command parser.
# GITHUB_APP_SLUG=my-dev-agent

# Optional: skip per-repo installation discovery by pinning the installation id.
# GITHUB_APP_INSTALLATION_ID=12345678

# Optional: fine-grained PAT fallback for git credentials when the App envs
# are absent (local development convenience — the App is the production path).
# GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_...

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev-agent time budget (docs/05-dev-agent.md, "Time budget discipline")
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Self-imposed budget for a nested dev-agent run, in ms. Default 700000
# (700s), clamped to a 750000 max in code — a Vercel Workflow step caps at
# ~800s, and a platform kill loses ALL partial work and triggers up to 3 step
# retries, each booting a fresh 8-vCPU sandbox. The clamp is deliberate; do
# not raise it.
# DEV_AGENT_TIME_BUDGET_MS=700000

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# eve channel sandbox lifecycle (docs/06-sandbox-lifecycle.md)
# NOTE: these govern eve's OWN per-session sandbox — a DIFFERENT lifecycle
# from the harness template snapshot below.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel Sandbox `timeout` for eve's session sandboxes: a HARD LIFETIME (the
# platform auto-terminates the VM this long after it starts; activity does not
# reset it). Session sandboxes are persistent, so the next access resumes the
# saved filesystem; only a command still running at that moment is lost.
# Default 30 minutes; values below 800000 (one tool-call step) are raised to
# it. The old name SANDBOX_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS is still accepted as an alias.
# SANDBOX_TIMEOUT_MS=1800000

# Default expiration of snapshots created for eve's sandboxes (the build-time
# template and the session sandboxes). Default 7 days. The TTL counts from the
# snapshot's last use; once eve's TEMPLATE snapshot lapses, new sessions cannot
# open a sandbox until you redeploy (docs/06-sandbox-lifecycle.md), so do not
# shorten it to save storage.
# SANDBOX_SNAPSHOT_EXPIRATION_MS=604800000

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Harness template snapshot lifecycle (distinct from the eve sandbox above!)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Expiration for the warm dev-agent template snapshot (the pre-built estate
# image forked per run). Default 7 days; the daily maintenance schedule
# re-warms it well before expiry.
# TEMPLATE_SNAPSHOT_EXPIRATION_MS=604800000

# Bump this to invalidate the cached template snapshot after ANY recipe
# change (CLI versions, estate additions, bootstrap steps). The bootstrap
# hash also covers the enabled repo@branch set, so estate flag flips
# auto-invalidate without a bump.
# RECIPE_VERSION=1

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Health alerts (optional — docs/07-ops.md)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by the external health-check workflow (GitHub Actions cron → Resend).
# These belong in GitHub Actions secrets/vars, NOT in the eve deployment —
# a dead agent cannot self-report. Listed here only for completeness.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# ALERT_EMAIL_FROM=agent-alerts@example.com
# ALERT_EMAIL_TO=you@example.com

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-run dev-task secrets (optional — docs/05-dev-agent.md, "Secret delivery")
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JSON map of secrets a dev-task run may need (e.g. test-account credentials).
# Delivered to the sandbox via session.run's env map and materialized as a
# tmp file — NEVER interpolated into prompts, command strings, or logs.
# DEV_TASK_SECRETS_JSON={"TEST_USER":"...","TEST_PASSWORD":"..."}

